body:
Not quite sure what I was doing by calling `RenderingServer::request_frame_drawn_callback` right after binding the callback, fixed the issue by editing this into:

```c++
void EditorResourcePreviewGenerator::DrawRequester::request_and_wait(RID p_viewport) {
	Callable request_prepare_draw = callable_mp(this, &EditorResourcePreviewGenerator::DrawRequester::_prepare_draw).bind(p_viewport);
	if (EditorResourcePreview::get_singleton()->is_threaded()) {
		if (!RS::get_singleton()->is_connected(SNAME("frame_pre_draw"), request_prepare_draw)) {
			RS::get_singleton()->connect(SNAME("frame_pre_draw"), request_prepare_draw, Object::CONNECT_ONE_SHOT);
		}
		semaphore.wait();

		...
```

Where `_prepare_draw` is written below:

```c++
void EditorResourcePreviewGenerator::DrawRequester::_prepare_draw(RID p_viewport) {
	RS::get_singleton()->viewport_set_update_mode(p_viewport, RSE::VIEWPORT_UPDATE_ONCE);
	RS::get_singleton()->request_frame_drawn_callback(callable_mp(this, &EditorResourcePreviewGenerator::DrawRequester::_post_semaphore));
}
```

The code change here is needed due to an attempt to call `request_and_wait` multiple times to redraw thumbnails for Materials and Meshes, which has known thumbnail render issues and can only be resolved by drawing it twice. (Just checked it today the issue still present if only drawn once)

